@BIND
.
=BIND
.
.BIND name = target gives a second name to a variable, an array, a constant,
.a SUB, a FUNCTION or a namespace. It costs nothing at run time.
.
:BIND G = GFX
:BIND P = GFX.PLOT
:BIND C = GFX.COLOR
:P(1, 2)
.
.  - The new name has the same mark as the target: BIND C$ = GFX.COLOR stops
.    the compile with BIND NEEDS THE SAME MARK.
.  - A BIND belongs to the scope it is written in. A BIND in a SUB is the
.    SUB's.
.  - A label cannot be bound.
.
.See Namespaces.
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>35|Namespaces
